<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The team and cycle analysis heavily favoured the Gadgeteer class, where it could independently gain full ownership through 1 panel and 2 balls. Since the Commander class could not score any confirmed points \(panel points could be overturned via loss of ownership\), the Gadgeteer could score confirmed points while gaining full ownership, making it an overall better pick. The adaptability of the Gadgeteer is also unmatched, where it scores both game pieces, allowing it to play effectively to the instantaneous needs of the team.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [5]
>>
