487 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (The final climbing mechanism was inspired by team 118's 2016 detachable climber and conventional rock climbing cams. The actual climbing mechanism resembles a trident and remains disconnected from the robot throughout gameplay to adhere to height restrictions, then attaches to the elevator via an 160 pound electromagnet during endgame. With this, the flat portion of the climber can reach a max height of about 65.5 inches. Then, a winch pulls down and rotates the cams on  each side of the trident, resulting in a very strong frictional hold. The winch continues operating, pulling the robot up after the cams clamp on.)
/E (The final climbing mechanism was inspired by team 118's 2016 detachable climber and conventional rock climbing cams. The actual climbing mechanism resembles a trident and remains disconnected from the robot throughout gameplay to adhere to height restrictions, then attaches to the elevator via an 160 pound electromagnet during endgame. With this, the flat portion of the climber can reach a max height of about 65.5 inches. Then, a winch pulls down and rotates the cams on  each side of the trident, resulting in a very strong frictional hold. The winch continues operating, pulling the robot up after the cams clamp on.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
